== Sabotage NOT RUN (owner decision, 2026-11-06) ==
The plan's SB11-a..f were not run. Writing audit/phase9/partb/b11_sabotage.py was stopped twice by the assistant's
own safety classifier (an environment limitation, not a test or tool failure); the script does not exist and no
sabotage was performed. Offered to the owner: run them yourself, or log the gap and continue. Owner: "Log the gap,
continue".
What this leaves unverified, stated plainly: that each of the six rules is actually load-bearing in a test. The
positive tests above pass, and the export comparison has its own positive control, but nothing here demonstrates that
a hand-edited figure (SB11-a), z = 1.645 (SB11-b), a dropped "not used for this result" label (SB11-c), a dropped
lower-bound caveat (SB11-d), a wrong-gene lookup (SB11-e) or a leak into the printable summary (SB11-f) would turn a
test red. Standing rule 4 ("every fix gets sabotage") is therefore not satisfied for B11, by owner decision, and this
is the only Part B item so far with no sabotage evidence. The six cases stay written in B11_PLAN.md so they can be run
later; audit/phase9/partb/b10_sabotage.py is the pattern.

